q_lines.append("### Question 3: Preservation of Claim-Level Clusters in Experiment 2 Bootstrap Resampling\n\n")
q_lines.append("**Audit Prompt:** *Does Experiment 2 correctly preserve claim-level clusters when resampling the 1,500 evidence evaluations?*\n\n")
q_lines.append("- **Severity:** Low / Pass (Cluster structure strictly preserved)\n")
q_lines.append("- **Exact File & Line Reference:**\n")
q_lines.append("  - `experiments/experiment2_formal.py`, lines 280–320\n")
q_lines.append("- **Relevant Code & Data Evidence:**\n")
q_lines.append("  In `experiments/experiment2_formal.py`:\n")
q_lines.append("  ```python\n")
q_lines.append("  # Group evidence rows by claim cluster\n")
q_lines.append("  claim_ids = df['claim_id'].unique() # M = 500 clusters\n")
q_lines.append("  claim_dict = {cid: df[df['claim_id'] == cid] for cid in claim_ids}\n")
q_lines.append("  ...\n")
q_lines.append("  for b in range(n_bootstraps):\n")
q_lines.append("      # Resample clusters with replacement\n")
q_lines.append("      sampled_cids = np.random.choice(claim_ids, size=len(claim_ids), replace=True)\n")
q_lines.append("      # Concatenate entire 3-row cluster for each sampled claim\n")
q_lines.append("      boot_df = pd.concat([claim_dict[cid] for cid in sampled_cids], ignore_index=True)\n")
q_lines.append("  ```\n")
q_lines.append("  At every replicate $b$, exactly 500 claims are sampled with replacement, and each sampled claim brings its complete triplet of 3 retrieved evidence passages (totaling exactly 1,500 rows per replicate). Intra-cluster correlation and within-claim ranking structures are 100% preserved.\n")
q_lines.append("- **Why it is a Problem (if verified):**\n")
q_lines.append("  Naively resampling 1,500 individual evidence rows would violate independence assumptions, destroy within-claim ranking constraints, and generate invalid standard error estimates. Cluster bootstrap at the claim level is the mathematically required procedure (Cameron et al., 2008).\n")
q_lines.append("- **Status:** Verified Fact (Correctly implemented).\n")
q_lines.append("- **Minimal Proposed Remedy:** Retain implementation; cite cluster bootstrap methodology in Phase 14 documentation.\n\n")

# Question 4
q_lines.append("### Question 4: Statistical Inference, Bootstrap P-Values, CIs, and Holm–Bonferroni Correction\n\n")
q_lines.append("**Audit Prompt:** *Are bootstrap p-values, confidence intervals, degenerate replicates, and Holm–Bonferroni corrections implemented exactly as specified?*\n\n")
q_lines.append("- **Severity:** Low / Pass (Correctly implemented according to approved protocol)\n")
q_lines.append("- **Exact File & Line Reference:**\n")
q_lines.append("  - `experiments/experiment2_formal.py`, lines 325–398\n")
q_lines.append("  - `outputs/phase11_formal/summary.json`, section `co_primary_results_dynamic_pipeline`\n")
q_lines.append("  - `outputs/phase11_formal/config.json`, line `\"n_bootstraps\": 1000`\n")
q_lines.append("- **Relevant Code & Data Evidence:**\n")
q_lines.append("  In `experiments/experiment2_formal.py`:\n")
q_lines.append("  - Null-Shift Centering: $\\tilde{\\Delta}^*_b = \\Delta^*_b - \\hat{\\Delta}$. Centering the bootstrap distribution around 0 enforces the null hypothesis $H_0: \\Delta = 0$.\n")
q_lines.append("  - Two-Sided Empirical P-Value:\n")
q_lines.append("    $$p = \\frac{1 + \\sum_{b=1}^{B_{\\text{valid}}} \\mathbb{I}(|\\tilde{\\Delta}^*_b| \\ge |\\hat{\\Delta}|)}{B_{\\text{valid}} + 1}$$\n")
q_lines.append("    With $B_{\\text{valid}} = 1,000$ and $B_{\\text{degenerate}} = 0$:\n")
q_lines.append("    - H1 (AUROC): $\\hat{\\Delta} = +0.0365$, raw $p = 0.0240$.\n")
q_lines.append("    - H2 (Average Precision): $\\hat{\\Delta} = -0.1396$, raw $p = 0.0010$.\n")
q_lines.append("  - Confidence Intervals: Computed via empirical percentiles:\n")
q_lines.append("    - 95% Marginal CI: $[q_{0.025}, q_{0.975}]$. For AUROC: $[0.0053, 0.0686]$. For AP: $[-0.1777, -0.1025]$.\n")
q_lines.append("    - 97.5% Bonferroni CI: $[q_{0.0125}, q_{0.9875}]$. For AUROC: $[0.00006, 0.0710]$. For AP: $[-0.1856, -0.0988]$.\n")
q_lines.append("  - Holm–Bonferroni Step-Down Procedure:\n")
q_lines.append("    Hypotheses ordered by raw p-value: $p_{(1)} = 0.0010$ (H2), $p_{(2)} = 0.0240$ (H1).\n")
q_lines.append("    - Step 1 (H2): Target $\\alpha / 2 = 0.025$. Adjusted $p = 2 \\times 0.0010 = 0.0020 < 0.025 \\implies$ Significant.\n")
q_lines.append("    - Step 2 (H1): Target $\\alpha / 1 = 0.050$. Adjusted $p = \\max(0.0020, 1 \\times 0.0240) = 0.0240 < 0.050 \\implies$ Significant.\n")
q_lines.append("    Family-wise error rate (FWER) is strictly controlled at $\\alpha = 0.05$.\n")
q_lines.append("- **Why it is a Problem (if verified):**\n")
q_lines.append("  Uncentered bootstrap p-values $2 \\min(P(\\Delta^* \\le 0), P(\\Delta^* \\ge 0))$ can be severely biased when the bootstrap distribution is skewed. The null-shifted pivot test correctly centers the distribution, ensuring exact Type I error control.\n")
q_lines.append("- **Status:** Verified Fact.\n")
q_lines.append("- **Minimal Proposed Remedy:** Clarify in reporting text that while the initial design proposal considered $B=2,000$, the formal frozen execution script used $B=1,000$ valid replicates as configured in `outputs/phase11_formal/config.json`.\n\n")

